competitors.description:
@P3b7_ that's true on MPC. you cannot simply make PQ-secure the consensus layer, add PQ signing on the userland side, and call it a day. There is plenty of work to be done on the wallet and custody infra side. When we started building @QuantumFDN, we took this into account from day 1, and we began researching PQ threshold sigs that can work well with MPC for asset custody. 

We landed on Mithril by PQShield, and it is now one of the main building blocks in our PQ signing co-processor for custody stacks.

you can check PQ wallet layer & some mithril details here: https://t.co/HbLirrHIeA

